      "message": "I\u0027m not sure about the approach of rejecting unknown elements and attributes. The bad: it\u0027ll prevent you from adding more elements/attributes in the future versions of Android platform. The good: it\u0027ll catch mistyped elements/attributes which would otherwise be ignored. Perhaps the latter can be addressed via Android Linter warnings instead?\n\nAlso, whenever you use getAttributeValue(namespace, name, defaultValue) you\u0027re not throwing if there are unknown/unexpected attributes in that element. Consistency needed.",
      "revId": "9ff20929e841a9514e6917db7ad1f3527ecd69a6",
